000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. PARMMAIN.
000300*A main program takes the EXEC PARM through its LINKAGE SECTION
000400*and PROCEDURE DIVISION USING, as IKFCBL00's does: R1 -> the
000500*halfword length and the text. The harness runs it with
000600*PARM='HELLO'. The program is compiled as one that may be called,
000700*so this also checks that its STOP RUN closes the runtime's
000800*SYSOUT itself. Expected output recorded from IBM ANS COBOL on
000900*TK5.
001000 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
001100 DATA DIVISION.
001200 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
001300 01  N PIC 99.
001400 LINKAGE SECTION.
001500 01  PARM-AREA.
001600     05  PARM-LEN  PIC S9(4) COMP.
001700     05  PARM-TEXT PIC X(20).
001800 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING PARM-AREA.
001900 MAIN-PARA.
002000     MOVE PARM-LEN TO N.
002100     DISPLAY 'LEN [' N ']'.
002200     DISPLAY 'TEXT [' PARM-TEXT ']'.
